Key takeaways for the experiment runner:
1. Closest prior art is MagicPIG (LSH sampling) and HashEvict (LSH eviction).
   Cold-Compress is the recommended integration point because HashEvict was
   released as a fork of it.
2. The single most important benchmark is RULER's cwe/fwe (aggregation tasks);
   prior LSH-TopK methods fail there even though they pass NIAH.
3. RetrievalAttention identifies an OOD problem between Q and K distributions
   that breaks naive ANN/LSH; SMYRF's asymmetric LSH is the canonical fix.
4. NSA (DeepSeek 2025) calls out non-differentiability of hard hashing as a
   training-time blocker; design accordingly.
5. The "adaptive KV quantization" half of the hypothesis pairs naturally with
   KIVI's per-channel-K / per-token-V scheme.
